{"base_rate":0.31414473684210525,"brier":0.2135018092105263,"bss":0.009078398433085999,"bss_hi":0.15336587305997598,"bss_lo":-0.17710990768593377,"chart":{"base":[469.3,77.8],"fp":[174.4,230.6],"lead":"62,157.3 272,137.3 482,138.4 692,130.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.01 — higher than 12% of cities","fp":"low end -2pp, high end +32pp","lead":"day-1 error 2.0 °C — better than 5% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 2%; promised 98% → rained 68%"},"rel":"67.4,458.7 194.8,422.4 408.3,350.1 582.9,259.1 681.2,172.4"},"country":"CD","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.21199013157894736,"ess":398.45794098550624,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Kinshasa</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Kinshasa rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>68%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 608 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 10.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.01, ranked 187 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(160&ndash;199) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>119</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'><b>15%</b></td><td class='num'>55</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>47%</td><td class='num'><b>20%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>64%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>57</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>77%</td><td class='num'><b>47%</b></td><td class='num'>60</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>59</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>68%</b></td><td class='num'>128</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 8 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Kinshasa</b> <span class=\"muted\">DR Congo</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.01</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>160&ndash;199\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>608 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Kinshasa &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Kinshasa\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\